      Attic Radiant Barrier Foil: Rafter Stapling &amp; Open Airspace Rules
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Radiant barrier foils do not possess an R-value; they do not slow down heat conduction like fiberglass or cellulose. Instead, they operate strictly on the physics of <strong>electromagnetic thermal radiation and surface emissivity</strong>. If installed without a dedicated open airspace or placed where dust can settle, a radiant barrier completely loses its thermal power. Here is how building science governs proper installation.
    </p>

