    avatarBg="bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800"
    initials="ER"
    title="Why Perforations are Non-Negotiable in Northern and Mixed Climate Zones"
    note="In southern Florida or Arizona (Climate Zone 1 and 2), moisture drive is predominantly exterior-to-interior. But in Climate Zones 3 through 7 (most of the United States), winter heating creates massive vapor drive from the warm living space upward into the cold attic. If you staple solid, non-perforated foil under your rafters, that warm household water vapor hits the cold foil, condenses into liquid droplets, and rains down onto your attic ceiling drywall! Perforated foil contains pinprick laser micro-holes spaced every 1/4 inch. These perforations allow water vapor molecules (which are sub-microscopic) to pass freely through to the ridge vent, while stopping long-wave infrared radiant heat waves (which are orders of magnitude larger). Always check that the roll specifies 'Perforated / Breathable' under ASTM E96."
  />

